## 1. Microservices Basics

### What are Microservices?

Microservices is an architectural style where an application is built as a collection of small, independent services that:
- Run in their own process
- Communicate via lightweight protocols (HTTP/REST, messaging)
- Are independently deployable
- Are organized around business capabilities

### Monolith vs Microservices

```
MONOLITHIC APPLICATION
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                 │
│   ┌─────────┬─────────┬─────────┬─────────┐   │
│   │  User   │ Product │  Order  │ Payment │   │
│   │ Module  │ Module  │ Module  │ Module  │   │
│   └─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴─────────┘   │
│                                                 │
│              SINGLE DATABASE                    │
│              SINGLE DEPLOYMENT                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

MICROSERVICES APPLICATION
┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐
│   User   │  │ Product  │  │  Order   │  │ Payment  │
│ Service  │  │ Service  │  │ Service  │  │ Service  │
└────┬─────┘  └────┬─────┘  └────┬─────┘  └────┬─────┘
     │             │             │             │
┌────▼─────┐  ┌────▼─────┐  ┌────▼─────┐  ┌────▼─────┐
│  User DB │  │Product DB│  │ Order DB │  │Payment DB│
└──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘
```

### Advantages of Microservices

| Advantage | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Independent Deployment** | Deploy one service without affecting others |
| **Technology Flexibility** | Use different languages/frameworks per service |
| **Scalability** | Scale only the services that need it |
| **Fault Isolation** | One service failure doesn't crash the entire system |
| **Team Autonomy** | Small teams can own and maintain their services |
| **Faster Development** | Parallel development by multiple teams |

### Disadvantages of Microservices

| Disadvantage | Description |
|--------------|-------------|
| **Complexity** | Distributed system is harder to manage |
| **Network Latency** | Service-to-service calls add latency |
| **Data Consistency** | Maintaining consistency across services is hard |
| **Testing** | End-to-end testing is more complex |
| **Monitoring** | Need specialized tools for observability |

