## 3. API Gateway

### What is API Gateway?

API Gateway is a single entry point for all client requests. It handles:
- Request routing
- Authentication & Authorization
- Rate limiting
- Load balancing
- Request/Response transformation

### Why Do We Need It?

```
WITHOUT API GATEWAY:
┌────────┐     ┌─────────────┐
│        │────►│Auth Service │ http://auth.example.com
│ Client │────►│Product Svc  │ http://product.example.com
│        │────►│Order Service│ http://order.example.com
└────────┘     └─────────────┘
Problems: Multiple URLs, no central security, CORS issues

WITH API GATEWAY:
┌────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐
│        │     │             │────►│Auth Service │
│ Client │────►│ API Gateway │────►│Product Svc  │
│        │     │             │────►│Order Service│
└────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘
               Single URL: api.example.com
```

### Gateway Responsibilities

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      API GATEWAY                            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                             │
│  1. ROUTING                                                 │
│     /api/v1/products/** → PRODUCT-SERVICE                  │
│     /api/v1/orders/**   → ORDER-SERVICE                    │
│     /api/v1/auth/**     → AUTH-SERVICE                     │
│                                                             │
│  2. AUTHENTICATION                                          │
│     • Validate JWT Token                                    │
│     • Extract user claims                                   │
│     • Reject unauthorized requests                          │
│                                                             │
│  3. LOAD BALANCING                                          │
│     • Distribute requests across instances                  │
│                                                             │
│  4. CROSS-CUTTING CONCERNS                                  │
│     • Logging                                               │
│     • Rate limiting                                         │
│     • CORS handling                                         │
│                                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Code Example

```yaml
# application.yml
spring:
  cloud:
    gateway:
      routes:
        - id: product-service
          uri: lb://PRODUCT-SERVICE  # lb = load balanced
          predicates:
            - Path=/api/v1/products/**
          filters:
            - AuthenticationFilter
```

