## 4. Feign Client

### What is Feign Client?

Feign is a declarative HTTP client that makes writing REST API clients easier. Instead of writing boilerplate code with RestTemplate, you define an interface and Feign handles the implementation.

### Without Feign (RestTemplate)

```java
// Verbose and error-prone
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final RestTemplate restTemplate;
    
    public ProductDTO getProduct(Long id) {
        String url = "http://PRODUCT-SERVICE/api/v1/products/" + id;
        ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<ProductDTO>> response = 
            restTemplate.exchange(
                url, 
                HttpMethod.GET, 
                null,
                new ParameterizedTypeReference<ApiResponse<ProductDTO>>() {}
            );
        return response.getBody().getData();
    }
}
```

### With Feign (Clean & Simple)

```java
// Define interface
@FeignClient(name = "PRODUCT-SERVICE")
public interface ProductClient {
    
    @GetMapping("/api/v1/products/{id}")
    ApiResponse<ProductDTO> getProductById(@PathVariable Long id);
}

// Use it
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final ProductClient productClient;
    
    public ProductDTO getProduct(Long id) {
        return productClient.getProductById(id).getData();
    }
}
```

### How Feign Works

```
┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐
│  Order Service  │     │  Feign Client   │     │ Product Service │
│                 │     │                 │     │                 │
│ productClient   │────►│ Creates HTTP    │────►│ GET /products/1 │
│ .getProductById │     │ request from    │     │                 │
│ (1)             │     │ interface       │     │ Returns JSON    │
│                 │◄────│ definition      │◄────│                 │
└─────────────────┘     └─────────────────┘     └─────────────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ Eureka Server   │
                    │ (Resolves       │
                    │ PRODUCT-SERVICE │
                    │ to IP:Port)     │
                    └─────────────────┘
```

