## 10. Synchronous vs Asynchronous Communication

### Synchronous (REST/Feign)

```
┌─────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐
│   Order     │ ─────► │  Product    │
│   Service   │        │  Service    │
│             │ ◄───── │             │
│ WAITS for   │        │             │
│ response    │        │             │
└─────────────┘        └─────────────┘

Use When:
✅ Need immediate response
✅ Simple request-response
✅ Real-time data needed

Example: Get product details for order
```

### Asynchronous (Kafka/RabbitMQ)

```
┌─────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐
│   Order     │ ─────► │   Message   │ ─────► │  Product    │
│   Service   │        │   Queue     │        │  Service    │
│             │        │             │        │             │
│ Continues   │        │             │        │ Processes   │
│ immediately │        │             │        │ later       │
└─────────────┘        └─────────────┘        └─────────────┘

Use When:
✅ Fire and forget
✅ Long-running tasks
✅ Decoupling needed
✅ High throughput

Example: Send notification email, generate report
```

